    "description": "Puget Sound Energy is a regulated electric and natural gas utility serving residential, commercial, and industrial customers in Washington. Public disclosures state that the company serves about 1.2 million electric customers and nearly 900,000 natural gas customers across a 6,000-square-mile territory in 10 counties. The operating model is asset-heavy and predominantly regulated, supported by generation, transmission, and distribution assets with revenues recovered through approved tariffs. Company materials describe owned and contracted hydro, wind, solar, natural gas, biomass, and other power resources, while BCI noted in September 2025 that PSE planned to phase out all coal-based electric generation by the end of 2025 and continue adding renewable and non-emitting resources. PSE was taken private in 2009 by a long-term infrastructure consortium that included BCI, and BCI's 2024 I&RR financial statements disclose a 20.9% ownership interest in Puget Sound Energy.",
